  "worked_solution": "From the equation of a plane in the parametric form $r=p+tv+sw$, we have that its normal vector is $n=v\\times w.$ In our case, the normal vector to $\u03a0$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =v\\times w \\\\  & =\u27e84,3,0\u27e9\\times \u27e80,2,5\u27e9 \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 4 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =15i-20j+8k \\\\  & =\u27e815,-20,8\u27e9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the plane $\u03a0$ in dot product form is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot \u27e815,-20,8\u27e9 & =\u27e810,-5,12\u27e9\\cdot \u27e815,-20,8\u27e9 \\\\ r\\cdot \u27e815,-20,8\u27e9 & =346.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=\u27e84,-2,3\u27e9+w\u27e85,-1,2\u27e9$ into the equation of the plane in dot product form, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot \u27e815,-20,8\u27e9 & =346 \\\\ \u27e84+5w,-2-w,3+2w\u27e9\\cdot \u27e815,-20,8\u27e9 & =346 \\\\ 15(4+5w)-20(-2-w)+8(3+2w) & =346 \\\\ 60+75w+40+20w+24+16w & =346 \\\\ 111w & =222 \\\\ w & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to get the position vector $q$ of the intersection point $Q,$ we substitute $w=2$ into the equation of the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}q & =\u27e84+5(2),-2-(2),3+2(2)\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e814,-4,7\u27e9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection point is $Q(14,-4,7).$",
